Readme ISO:

The Post-Mechanical keyboard has a writing core with 48 character keys. The extra key makes the keyboard ISO-compatible.

Most European language keyboards are built on the ISO standard.

This ISO US(English) Microsoft driver allows writers to use the ISO firmwared Dvorak keyboard in a normal manner. Using an ISO firmwared keyboard with the native Microsoft US(English) driver swaps the "[" and "]" pair (in the numbers-row) with the "-" and "=" (in the top-alpha row).

